## On the vision

Two observations for the owner, the useful kind:

- **BL-15 had no natural statement to lean on.** I used V1 (a video misclassified as a Short exits the corpus before the product can see it), which is honest but stretched — the vision says nothing about operational signal quality, i.e. that a check which cries wolf is worse than no check. AGENTS.md carries that ethos; the vision doesn't. If unattended runs keep producing warning/reporting-hygiene rulings, one sentence about alarms needing to mean something would give them a real anchor.
- **The V4/V10 boundary worked exactly as designed** for OD-13: OD-5 leaned on V10 to cap, the owner's amendment made clear V4 governs once density is *measured* (the 80% ratio), and V10 only governs unmeasured no-signal material. That reading is now recorded in OD-13's against-field; if it's wrong, V10 is the sentence to edit.
